{{!-- The membership CTA for the LIBRARY pages.

     The sitewide one (partials/membership-cta) is written for the
     moment a reader finishes an essay: "Loved this essay? Help us write
     the next one." That is the right copy under a post and nonsense at
     the foot of a reading room, where the reader has not read an essay
     and is not being asked to commission another. Ian pulled it from
     the three research tools on 2026-09-11 for exactly that reason;
     this replaces it on the twenty browse, reading-room and shelf pages
     where it was the only membership prompt there was.

     Same gate as the sitewide partial, deliberately: hidden from paid
     and comped members, shown to free members and to anonymous
     visitors. Reading is free and stays free, so a free member is still
     somebody this is written for.

     Not to be used under a post. The sitewide partial is still correct
     there and is untouched. --}}
{{#match @member.status "paid"}}{{else}}
{{#match @member.status "comped"}}{{else}}{{#match @member.status "gift"}}{{else}}
<section class="membership-cta">
    <div class="cta-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Faith Received</p>
        <h2><em>Free to read, and paid for by readers.</em></h2>
        <p>
            Every text here is free, and it stays free. What membership pays for is the work behind it: the translating, the scanning, and the years of putting a library like this within reach. Members also get the print journal, the full archive, and the research tools.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-buttons">
            <a href="/membership/" class="btn btn-solid btn-primary btn-lg">Become a Member</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
{{/match}}{{/match}}
{{/match}}
